<node id="11134459" title="Re: Using 'keys' on a list" created="2021-06-29 14:40:26" updated="2021-06-29 14:40:26" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="1172229">tybalt89</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;
At 5 characters
&lt;c&gt;
my @keys = keys %{{f}};
&lt;/c&gt;
is much more elegant than the equivalent
&lt;c&gt;
use List::Util qw( shuffle uniq pairkeys );
my @keys = shuffle uniq pairkeys f;
&lt;/c&gt;
Remember that hashes do uniq'ing and shuffling for free :)
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
UPDATE: added a missed "keys" as LanX pointed out.
&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
